ription \\\"QA description text\\\", deadline 2026-09-05, High priority, prerequisite \\\"Buy groceries\\\". Card renders: 'QA Full Task / High / QA description text / Sep 5 / Prerequisite \\\"Buy groceries\\\" incomplete'.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Edited unblocked \\\"QA Simple Task\\\": title→\\\"QA Simple Task Edited\\\", description→\\\"edited description\\\", deadline→2026-09-20 (renders \\\"Sep 20\\\"), priority→Low, prerequisites→QA Full Task + Schedule dentist appointment; all changes persisted on the card. Deleting it removed it from the task views (element absent) and counts went 6 active→5 active with completed unchanged at 3.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Completed eligible active task \\\"Buy groceries\\\": counts moved 7 active/2 completed → 6 active/3 completed, it left the active list and appears in the completed view. Completing \\\"QA Full Task\\\" then gave 5 active/4 completed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Active view (Active 7) listed only the 7 active/blocked tasks; clicking filters.show-completed (selected) shows only the 2 completed tasks (Reply to client emails, Organize desk) matching \\\"Completed 2\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Assigned two prerequisites (QA Full Task + Schedule dentist appointment) to QA Simple Task via edit form; saved card renders \\\"2 prerequisites incomplete\\\" and the task is now in blocked state. Single-prereq assignment also retained on QA Full Task ('Prerequisite \\\"Buy groceries\\\" incomplete').\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Blocked tasks (4, 7, QA Full Task) render with dashed warning border + muted background (bg-muted/30 border-dashed border-warning/40), complete toggle state=\\\"blocked\\\" and disabled=true, plus a blocked-warning label. Unblocked task 3 has normal border and enabled complete toggle.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Task 4 (one incomplete prereq) shows 'Prerequisite \\\"Review project proposal\\\" incomplete'; task 7 (two incomplete prereqs) shows \\\"2 prerequisites incomplete\\\"; QA Full Task shows 'Prerequisite \\\"Buy groceries\\\" incomplete'.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"While prerequisite \\\"Buy groceries\\\" was incomplete, QA Full Task's complete toggle was state=\\\"blocked\\\", disabled=true (click impossible). After completing Buy groceries, QA Full Task became state=\\\"active\\\" with an enabled toggle and showed \\\"1 prerequisite completed\\\"; clicking it then completed the task (counts 6/3 → 5/4).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Editing \\\"Review project proposal\\\" (1): prerequisite list omits itself and its dependents 4 and 7. Editing \\\"Buy groceries\\\" (3) with chain Buy groceries→QA Full Task→QA Simple Task Edited: list shows only 1,2,4,5,6,7 — omitting itself, direct dependent QA Full Task, and indirect dependent QA Simple Task Edited. Cycle-forming options are not offered.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"With whitespace-only title \\\"   \\\", task.form.submit remains enabled:false; pressing Enter did not create a task; tasks.summary stayed \\\"5 active, 2 completed\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After completion, \\\"Buy groceries\\\" and \\\"QA Full Task\\\" persist in the completed view (Completed 4) with full details (priority, deadline, prerequisite summary) and retain both a toggle-complete control (to reopen) and a delete control; nothing was auto-deleted.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Reopening a prerequisite leaves its completed dependent simultaneously completed and blocked, and the dependent becomes unrecoverable (all controls disabled except delete).\", \"actual\": \"\\\"QA Full Task\\\" (completed, prerequisite \\\"Buy groceries\\\") stayed completed after Buy groceries was reopened. The reopen was neither prevented nor did it reset the dependent: QA Full Task still appears in the Completed view (counts 6 active / 3 completed), title still line-through with complete state=\\\"completed\\\", while simultaneously displaying the blocked warning 'Prerequisite \\\"Buy groceries\\\" incomplete'. Its complete toggle is now disabled=true and edit disabled=true, so the user cannot un-complete or fix it — a permanently invalid completed+blocked state.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Dashed SVG connectors (stroke-dasharray 6px,4px) have pointer-events-auto/cursor-pointer hit paths (stroke-width 16). Hovering one sets data-state=\\\"delayed-open\\\" and opens role=tooltip: \\\"Dependency Chain — Submit final report (pending), Review project proposal (pending), Complete tax filing (pending)\\\", showing the chain and each task's completion state.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Hovering tasks.list.item.7.blocked-warning (\\\"2 prerequisites incomplete\\\") opens a tooltip (aria-describedby radix tooltip, cursor-help) reading \\\"Dependency Chain / Review project proposal – pending / Complete tax filing – pending\\\", naming both still-pending prerequisites.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Every task shows title + priority badge (e.g. \\\"Buy groceries\\\"/Low). QA Full Task shows description \\\"QA description text\\\" and deadline \\\"Sep 5\\\"; QA Simple Task (no description/deadline) omits both. Blocked tasks expose blocked-warning (e.g. 'Prerequisite \\\"Review project proposal\\\" incomplete'). Completed task title computed style textDecorationLine=line-through with muted color, distinguishing it from active tasks.\"}]}"
