    "content": "All 19 checklist items have been tested and recorded — coverage is complete.\n\n**Summary: 17 PASS / 2 FAIL**\n\nThe core to-do functionality is solid: task creation with full details, editing, deletion, completion with retention, active/completed views with accurate counts, priority and deadline sorting (undated tasks last), whitespace-title rejection, cycle prevention (both direct and indirect dependents excluded from the prerequisite picker), blocked-task styling and warnings, and both hover tooltips (dashed connector and blocked warning) showing the dependency chain with per-task pending state.\n\nTwo defects found:\n\n- **FT-3 (FAIL)** — On a blocked task the edit button is fully disabled and no alternative affordance exists, so description and priority cannot be modified. The requirement is that title and deadline are locked while description and priority stay editable.\n- **CS-22 (FAIL)** — Reopening a prerequisite of a completed dependent leaves that dependent in an invalid *completed **and** blocked* state. \"QA Full Task\" remained in the Completed view (still counted as completed, line-through) while displaying `Prerequisite \"Buy groceries\" incomplete`, and both its complete and edit controls became disabled — making the state unrecoverable short of deleting the task.\n\nOne methodology note: the dashed SVG connector for IX-18 has a zero-width bounding box, so Playwright's `browser_hover` refused it as \"not visible\". I verified it by dispatching genuine pointer events onto its 16px-wide transparent hit path; the tooltip opened normally (`data-state=\"delayed-open\"`), so this is a tooling limitation rather than an app defect."
